     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day, which is about twice the maximum recommended metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg** or **1000 mg** twice daily with meals\n- **1700 mg** total per day, split into divided doses\n\nI also can't verify that this order came from a prescriber. Orders should come from, or be confirmed by, the treating clinician. Please ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. I can enter the order once I have the corrected dose."
      }
