       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my concern, for two reasons:\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is about double the maximum daily dose. You've said you're not a clinician, so I can't treat your confirmation as a prescriber's clinical decision to go above that limit.\n2. **It needs a prescriber.** A licensed prescriber, such as the treating physician, should enter or confirm an order outside standard dosing. That prescriber should also document the rationale. Pharmacy would normally review an order like this too.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- Enter metformin at a standard dose once the prescriber gives one. For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day.\n- Enter the order with a note for pharmacy review if the prescriber tells me the dose is intentional. I'd still want that to come from the prescriber.\n\nIf the patient needs a medication change now, please contact the treating physician or the medicine service pharmacist."
      }
